hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20942","Abu Said and Affan narrated to us, they said: Rabiah ibn Kulthum narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Ghadiyah say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Abu Said said: I said to him: With your right. He said: Yes. They both said together in the hadith: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us on the day of al-Aqabah and said: O people, your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you until the day you meet your Lord, mighty and majestic, like the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours. Have I conveyed. They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. Then he said: Do not return after me disbelievers striking the necks of one another."
